/*! \page page_cli AnCH CLI library documentation
 *
 * \tableofcontents
 *
 * \section cli_intro_seq Introduction
 *
 * AnCH CLI library aims to provide facilities for parsing CLI arguments and CLI formatter
 *
 * \section cli_prereq_sec Prerequisites
 *
 * AnCH CLI is a standalone library for now
 *
 * \section cli_install_sec Installation
 *
 * CMake target \c anch::cli:
 * \code{.cmake}
find_package(Anch REQUIRED)
target_link_libraries(my-app PRIVATE anch::cli)
\endcode
 * See \ref install_sec "installation".
 *
 * \section cli_concept_sec Conception
 *
 * AnCH CLI library main class is: \ref anch::cli::ArgHandler "ArgHandler".\n
 * AnCH CLI library contains common bindings in \c cli/utils.hpp : invalid values (numbers which are empty, malformed or
 * out of range, files which can not be opened) raise \c std::invalid_argument , reported by \c ArgHandler::handle .\n
 * An option value is always the next argument (\c -p \c value or \c --plop \c value ): \c --plop=value and \c -pvalue
 * forms are not supported.\n
 * Multiple positional argument has to be the last positional argument. Options without value can be repeated ; options
 * with value can be repeated only when they are declared as \c multi .\n
 * The first \c -- ends options (POSIX convention): next arguments, \c -- included, are positional arguments.\n
 *\n
 * Console formatting (\ref anch::cli::Formatter "Formatter") is disabled when standard output is not a terminal, when
 * \c NO_COLOR environment variable is set and not empty, when \c ANCH_CLI_NO_FMT is \c 1 or with \c --no-term-fmt option.
 *
 * \section cli_example_sec Examples
 *
 * Generate and parse CLIs:
 * \snippet{trimleft} anch-cli/examples/cli.cpp example
 */
